<div class="container">
 
   <h2>What Is KitePHP?</h2>
   <p>KitePHP is a tiny, self-contained PHP framework designed to:</p>
   <ul>
    <li>Run on shared hosting with no shell access (like InfinityFree).</li>
    <li>Use no Composer on the server (a hand-rolled autoloader is bundled).</li>
    <li>Keep one app per project — no multi-tenant routing.</li>
    <li>Favor convention over configuration — folder names, namespace names, and file names must match exactly.</li>
   </ul>
 <p>It provides just enough structure to build small MVC apps:</p>
 <ul>
    <li>A front controller (index.php) that handles every request.</li>
    <li>A router that maps METHOD /path to a controller method.</li>
    <li>A base controller that renders views from apps/Views/.</li>
    <li>A template stubs system so php console make:apps can scaffold a fresh app.</li>   
    </ul>
     <p>KitePHP is intentionally small. It's meant to be read, modified, and understood — not to compete with Laravel or Symfony.</p>
</div>
